' covers: e2e/dashboard_sbx_tmux_test.go
' status: implemented. The HTML prototype that chose the layout (index.html,
' served by vite) was retired 2026-11-28 once the decisions were taken; the
' native Go dashboard implements Review queue with lower-right task details.
' Task graph, Schedule and alternate details are keyboard-selectable.
' Stock sbx parity and Fresh still need an authenticated guest run.
' Join scheduled tasks by stable job keys or explicit instance IDs.
' Ad hoc titles can repeat and do not establish task ownership.
' New scheduled instances mount a private per-attempt handoff directory
' for report.md so sibling jobs never consume each other's reports.
' Current lifecycle: _spec/internal/sbx/instance-lifecycle.puml
' Current state transfer: _spec/internal/sbx/state-sync.puml
' Earlier retention direction: _spec/_plans/session-continuity.puml
' Resource admission: _spec/internal/schedule/resource-queue.puml
' Delivery order and verification: _spec/_plans/dashboard-delivery.puml
'
' IDENTITY AND ISOLATION
' Keep canonical effective pwd as the workspace key, with explicit input and
' scope taking precedence. List any number of logical instances under that
' workspace, subject to machine capacity and scheduling limits. Generate an
' immutable instance ID for each new instance. Store target, optional label,
' optional task reference and selected Git base alongside it. Name the VM
' agent-task-shortid, at most 32 ASCII characters in total. Use a ticket key
' or slug for the task and adhoc when absent. Reserve the agent and suffix
' before truncating the task slug. Allocate a different suffix if a name
' already exists. Keep the allocated name when the title changes, and bind
' the instance record to the daemon-reported VM ID. Discover new Proveo VMs
' from their records and use the proveo- prefix for legacy discovery.
' Example: codex-prv-284-history-83f91a.
' Every launch creates a separate attempt ID. A task can own several instances.
' Sample CLI: proveo run codex --new --task PRV-284; proveo run codex --instance ID.
' One host lease per instance covers restore through final save and removal.
' Different instances run concurrently. One native session has one writer.
' Git work uses one private sbx clone per instance from a recorded commit.
' Check out the recorded base inside the guest and give it its own branch.
' Resolve the Git source separately from the agent cwd. Preserve any scope
' restrictions when preparing the guest checkout.
' Fetch the base by ref or stage a Git bundle when the ref is unavailable.
' Carry results under per-attempt refs. Keep host edits in the host checkout.
' Use an explicit snapshot when the operator wants uncommitted input.
' Seed isolated writes from a snapshot for a non-Git directory. Export
' results under the attempt ID.
' Shared writable direct mode permits one writer over overlapping host paths.
' Reject a second writer or require a private copy. Distinct VMs can still
' share dependencies through read-only mounts and contend for host ports.
' CHOSEN BRANCH (2026-11-27): an instance records WorkBranch when its run passed
' --branch; Branch() then names it instead of proveo/<name>, and allocation
' fetches it from origin and starts from its tip when origin has it. A proveo/*
' branch's upstream is itself in the checkout, so it stays local.
' LINKED SHARES (2026-11-27, chosen "Always writable"): an escaping symlink the
' workspace plan mounts, such as the monorepo's _spec -> ~/Syncd/pluvo/_spec,
' keeps the workspace's mode in an isolated instance instead of being forced
' read-only; the seed demands _spec writable, so the forced mode made every new
' instance exit 1 ("_spec is read-only, so edits cannot reach the host"). Parallel
' instances may edit the same spec file; Syncd keeps conflict copies. A run with
' --read-only-shares (reviews) still mounts them read-only (instanceMounts).
'
' RESUME AND RETENTION
' Save instance records and a host index under the existing state root.
' Resume identifies the instance and the exact harness-native session ID.
' Restore the selected state and Git ref into a clean guest before launch.
' Each instance records its last verified native session. An explicit
' native session ID can select an earlier session in that instance.
' Reuse a matching VM only when its ID and launch receipt match and it has
' no live owner. A disposable VM can resume the same logical instance.
' Keep the current single-instance shortcut where one candidate exists.
' With several candidates, --continue opens a picker, or reports required
' selection in noninteractive use. Scheduled jobs pin an instance or ask
' for a new one. Migrate a legacy workspace key into one default instance.
' Use only a trusted listing when binding that record to an existing VM.
'
' HISTORY ON MANAGED EXIT
' Record the attempt before launch. After any managed agent exit, including
' a failed attempt or requested stop, try to publish its native session
' checkpoint and result. Git carry and history save have their own status.
' Export per instance into private staging. Verify manifest and payload,
' then fsync and atomically publish an immutable checkpoint on the host.
' Update the instance head after publication. Retry is idempotent by
' attempt and checkpoint ID. An older attempt cannot replace a newer head.
' Periodic safe checkpoints reduce loss on host crash, forced kill or VM
' deletion. A failed final save leaves the last good checkpoint and keeps
' the VM for recovery when it still exists. Show retry needed or missing.
' Disk full, guest unreachability and permission errors can block an export.
' Preserving history and carrying work are independent. Remove the VM only
' after both have succeeded or the operator explicitly discards the residue.
' Raw sbx stop or removal can bypass the managed exit path. Reconcile the
' daemon inventory and try to recover surviving VMs. Raw sbx removal
' before a checkpoint can destroy the only copy. Unmanaged sandboxes have
' no Proveo session contract. Deduplicate repeated exports on retry.
'
' HARNESS EXPORT CONTRACTS
' Claude Code: carry this instance's projects and verified native session
' records. sessions/ contains live process registrations. Keep it and
' daemon locks, sockets and status files in the guest.
' Codex: persist rollout JSONL and verify native resume from the host index.
' Probe whether the pinned version needs SQLite metadata restored as well.
' Cursor: verify its pinned native chat export and resume format before
' offering resume from a rebuilt VM. Show transcript availability separately.
' OpenCode: existing replacement exports the engine database as a SQLite
' backup. OpenCode v2 mixes credentials and history in that database. Use
' native session export/import for portable resume. A local v2.4.1 probe
' exported a session as JSON, imported it into a blank store at another
' directory, and found it by the original ID. The sanitized export redacted
' the title. Test message and child-session round trips in sbx before
' replacing retained engines. Keep full resume archives private and use
' redacted evidence for review. The session list filters by project, so
' check for the native ID before treating an empty list as data loss.
' Hermes: current durable HERMES_HOME is shared. Parallel copies need a
' per-instance home so state.db and gateway sockets have a single owner.
' Decide separately how personal memory can travel between instances.
' Across all harnesses, validate native IDs, paths and restore version.
' Keep credentials, auth stores and live process state out of the archive.
'
' DASHBOARD AND HANDOFF
' Bare proveo on an interactive terminal opens Proveo and sbx tabs. Keep
' help available via --help and on noninteractive invocation. Show the
' effective pwd next to the tabs and keep the switch hint visible. Run
' stock sbx in a PTY sized to its content pane. The multiplexer handles
' Ctrl+G then Tab switches views. Ctrl+C in Proveo opens the shared
' confirmation card with Cancel selected. Exit closes the dashboard.
' Ctrl+C in the sbx view exits directly.
' View switches keep the outer dimensions and the running child.
' Match the left-pane column count after observing the child divider.
' Before a divider is visible, use 30 percent of the available columns.
' Scroll within each pane. Resize
' the child PTY on actual terminal resize.
' Bubble Tea v2 owns the model, input and outer alternate screen. Lip Gloss
' v2 composes the panes using the existing internal/ui identity roles.
' Bubbles v2 key and help draw the bottom key bar from the active bindings.
' Follow the sbx footer pattern with a bright key and a muted action.
' Show ↵ Attach in the dashboard footer and ↵ Open file for file rows.
' Use cyan for the shortcut and muted text for the action.
' Mark selection with a cyan cursor and a subtle tint. Keep status colors
' visible. Put the HTML preview's layout picker, task detail options,
' and implementation guide below the terminal frame. Separate task groups
' and panes with rules. Keep task rows compact and graph nodes unboxed.
' Reuse creack/pty and x/term primitives on Unix. Evaluate Charm x/vt for
' the child screen buffer, alternate screen, cursor, and terminal replies.
' The native Go dashboard pins x/vt with Ultraviolet and ANSI.
' A local probe exercised alternate-screen entry, restore and resizing.
' [Unverified] Native sbx behavior under the embedded emulator.
' Keep native output within the pane and route its replies to the child.
' Windows needs a ConPTY adapter. The existing ptyproxy Windows path is a
' stub. Show the embedded sbx view when a platform has an adapter.
' A confirmed exit and an external SIGINT take the same shutdown path. Close
' the dashboard-owned sbx client with a bounded wait, restore terminal
' state, and exit with status 130. Keep running sandboxes and scheduled jobs.
' TASK DETAILS, MEASURED AND FIXED 2026-11-25 (macOS, sbx v0.54.0):
'   usage ..... the probe pinned -u agent -w <computed guest path> and ran only
'               for instances with a Workdir and Host, so a discovered sandbox
'               always read "—". Now: sbx exec SANDBOX -- sh -c probe, no user
'               or workdir, behind verifiedGuest (sbx ls says running) so a
'               stopped VM never restarts; CPU cores busy of nproc, RAM used of
'               MemTotal, disk, /proc/uptime. A discovered sandbox is Guest with
'               the host's name and its first sbx ls workspace as Workdir.
'               sbx inspect and sbx ls report no usage (checked).
'   files ..... Files listed the host checkout. Now the task's sandbox:
'               guest git ls-files (find outside git), else git ls-tree of the
'               carried tip, else of the base. Changes read the guest's diff
'               against the base plus untracked files, or its git status.
'               Guest git runs with GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0: the agent works there.
'   base ...... Changes are a PR's view: the diff from where the branch left its
'               base, uncommitted work and untracked files included, the way
'               `git diff origin/dev...HEAD` reads (never HEAD..origin/dev, which
'               adds what landed on dev since). The base is, in order: the PR's
'               baseRefName from gh; else the candidate with the fewest commits
'               since its merge base among the host repo's origin/HEAD and
'               origin/dev, develop, main, master, trunk, skipping origin/<own
'               branch>; else the recorded launch commit. A PR found later
'               re-reads the changes against its base.
'               MEASURED 2026-11-25: inside an sbx clone origin is GitHub but
'               origin/HEAD names the task's own branch (rs-ashby-tipalti), so
'               the clone's default is never trusted; origin/dev was 11 commits
'               back, origin/main 55. The dashboard read 33 files vs origin/dev;
'               gh pr view 3949 reported baseRefName dev and 33 changedFiles.
'   PR ........ gh pr list --head <branch> --state all (fork PRs dropped, open
'               first), once per working branch; every branch keeps its PR, so a
'               stacked pair shows both. No commit lookup: gh api .../commits/
'               <sha>/pulls named PRs that merely contain a shared commit.
'   work ...... the branches come from where the agent works, not from the
'               mount: sbx exec starts in the workspace, so the probe cds to /
'               first or it counts itself. It reads /proc/*/cwd, ranks the git
'               top levels of claude, codex, opencode, cursor-agent and hermes
'               processes first, the rest by process count, and lists each
'               top's nested worktrees after it; the mount is the fallback. The
'               carried proveo/<instance> branch is asked last.
'               MEASURED 2026-11-25, five running sandboxes: 1b3fcb7f claude in
'               worktrees/dev on rs-cloud-accounts-ui (#3975) with nested
'               .claude/worktrees/rs-cloud-revoke-reach (#3974), its mount on
'               rs-ashby-tipalti (#3949, another sandbox's PR) holding only the
'               probe; 9995ea77 worktrees/hotfix rs-projector (#3976);
'               36915573 worktrees/main rs-teamwork (#3937); 8abaedd2 monorepo
'               rs-ashby-tipalti (#3949). The usage probe carries this read, so
'               every running sandbox is sampled in turn on a 2 s tick: the
'               selected one when its sample is 5 s old, else the next one
'               whose sample is 15 s old, else none.
'   activity .. the same probe reads each agent's own state and proveo's hook
'               markers; idle and waiting agents move to Attention required.
'               See _spec/packages/lib/agent-activity.puml.
'               No gh or no auth shows "install gh for PR status" or
'               "gh auth login for PR status", as Claude Code's footer does.
'               Cached a minute per task, branch and tip. MEASURED: PR #3949
'               found for a discovered monorepo sandbox through its guest branch.
'               Sources: Claude Code CHANGELOG 2.1.20, 2.1.145, 2.1.248, 2.1.251,
'               2.1.326 and code.claude.com/docs/en/interactive-mode#pr-review-status;
'               Codex codex-rs/tui/src/branch_summary.rs (gh pr view, then the
'               head commit's pulls); OpenCode shows the branch only;
'               cli.github.com/manual/gh_pr_list.
'   PR scan ... the PR's title, body, head branch and files name the work.
'               Linear: linear.app links, closing words (Fixes, Closes, Resolves,
'               Part of, Related to, Refs), the title, a user/abc-123 branch,
'               then bare IDs in prose ("Requested in CONN-116 and CONN-114"),
'               look-alikes such as UTF-8 and SHA-256 dropped. The first is
'               fetched from Linear when LINEAR_API_KEY is set. Plan: the body's
'               "Plan: <link or path>" line, which AGENTS.md now asks every PR
'               description to end with; else a _spec/_plans path or link; else
'               a changed _spec/_plans file. Any .md is a plan. A discovered
'               sandbox takes its PR's title. Every card's PR is read one at a
'               time and cached a minute. MEASURED: PR #3949 gave its title,
'               CONN-116 and CONN-114.
'   ticket .... a sandbox name like proveo-claudecode-36915573 read as ticket
'               CLAUDECODE-36915573; a ticket label now needs a real ticket.
' Restore the start termios with an input flush (TCSAFLUSH), not a plain set.
' MEASURED 2026-11-25 on macOS: Ctrl+C on the sbx tab quit with terminal
' replies still queued, the canonical restore set PENDIN, and the shell would
' retype them; TestNativeDashboardTabsOnTmux saw it as stty drift.
' If the sbx client exits independently, show its status in Proveo. Never
' start a fallback shell in the sbx pane.
' Proveo joins agent, Git and task data. Discover running sandboxes that
' report effective pwd as their primary workspace. A discovered row has
' no Proveo owner, task, or attach action until a separate record links it.
' Local plans and explicit ticket URLs remain valid task sources.
' The host dashboard reads Linear GraphQL using LINEAR_API_KEY.
' A ticket URL or key selects its issue. A key in a branch or task name
' links only after the API confirms the issue. The existing scheduler and result store
' supply attempt outcomes, time budget, reports and carried refs.
' Task details pairs the Git provider and task source in its heading.
' Lead task details with CPU utilization, RAM in use, and disk in use for
' the selected attempt's sandbox. Show the last observed sample after
' exit. Show placeholders for absent samples and distinguish requested
' resources from measured usage.
' Read the selected running sandbox on selection and every 5s on the
' Proveo tab. The same probe discovers Fresh while details are closed.
' Resolve its recorded sbx ID on the owning host.
' Bound reads to one in flight and discard replies for an earlier selection.
' The sbx inventory reader verifies local VM identity. The live probe uses
' ps, /proc/meminfo and df in the recorded guest workdir as user agent.
' Live guest verification of those measurements is pending.
' The HTML preview polls sample telemetry.
' Show ticket, branch, instance, sandbox, and PR above the prompt.
' Clip the task-source description to three rows with an ellipsis. Show
' the latest observed branch push as a local date and time in smaller,
' muted text. Keep run controls outside the scrolling task details.
' End task details with the initial prompt. Show the current phase in
' the queue row.
' Fit complete visual rows into the prompt preview. Mark overflow and
' allow the reader to scroll the prompt.
' New instance hands the terminal to `proveo run --queue`: the same harness
' list (running tasks left out), scope page and choice card as `proveo run`.
' DECIDED 2026-11-25 by the Executor: same card, queued, then attach.
' The card's answers reach the settings cache, and the scheduled run replays
' them under --yes; flags the operator typed, and the scope, ride as job Args.
' The job is mode attended: no budget, no report stop, an opening prompt only
' if one was given. It waits up to 20s for admission, then attaches; Ctrl+B d
' returns to the dashboard. Still queued, it says why and hands back.
' Prompt-first overnight work stays with schedule.yml and the CLI.
' A task can supply a prompt template. Review the chosen target, sandbox
' name, and prompt before launch. Store the submitted prompt with the
' instance's first attempt. Task details displays that snapshot even if
' the task or prompt file is edited later. Deliver the prompt through the
' runner's input path.
' The left pane defaults to Changes for the selected task. Record its
' Git base and the exact feature-branch tip carried for the selected
' attempt. Group paths from git diff --name-status -z -M <base> <tip>.
' Use a slightly smaller type size in the HTML file tree to preserve
' more of each path within its column.
' Existing clone teardown snapshots dirty work and applies its carry to
' refs/proveo/<run-id>/<branch>. Keep the last carried revision visible
' during a live run, with its age. Report when no snapshot has arrived.
' Retain referenced Git objects for as long as their reviews are visible.
' Enter on a live scheduled task opens a confirmation using the post-exit
' dialog style. Name the agent session and its task in the body.
' Offer Cancel as the default and Attach to invoke
' proveo attach <job>. Report when no job is live.
' Return to the same dashboard view when the child client detaches.
' Preserve selection, focus, and scroll. The HTML demo models direct
' attach and detaches with Ctrl+B then d. The agent keeps running.
' An existing tmux client uses its prefix then L to switch back after
' proveo attach switches its session. Nested read-only attach and zellij
' use the sequences documented in proveo attach --help.
' Enter on a file opens the editor pane across the center and right.
' Keep the tree visible. Read changed files from the recorded tip and
' deleted files from the base. Read both sides whole and colour them: p file
' or diff, u unified, i side by side, [ ] previous or next file; see
' dashboard-terminal-design.puml (preview).
' Mark deleted files in Changes with Proveo's red D and a struck-through
' filename.
' Preserve filename extensions and identifier suffixes when clipping.
' Keep the full values available and show the opened file's full path.
' Use f for Files in the effective host pwd and g for carried Changes.
' Show the highlighted key first in f See files and g See changes.
' Offer e (Fresh) for the selected task when its sandbox is running and
' Fresh is available in the guest's workspace. Resolve the sandbox's
' recorded identity and guest workdir. Launch Fresh with interactive sbx
' exec on the owning host as the run user. Restore task details when it exits.
' Hide the binding when the sandbox or editor is unavailable. The HTML
' preview uses a distinct read-only file tree for the running sample.
' Fresh's worktree-based Orchestrator stays outside this design.
' Disk capacity and prerequisite changes admit queued tasks. Calendar jobs can
' submit work for overnight runs. Review connects agent, ticket, spec,
' evidence, ref and session.
' Task stages: spec -> verification -> spec -> live verification (repeat)
' -> upgrade -> PR -> review -> merge. Review feedback can reopen the loop.
' Evidence attaches to the exact tested revision. A revision change reopens
' affected verification. The operator controls posting and merging the PR.
' View 1 groups Attention required, Working and Queued. Place n new
' instance in an outlined item below the queued tasks. It opens the
' same proveo run --queue by shortcut or item activation. View 2 draws
' prerequisite-to-dependent paths and explicit extra edges. Validate IDs
' and cycles before dispatch. Order the paths deterministically. Fold
' long sections into a count such as "3 tasks", with expansion on demand.
' Measure the terminal width for the path row, preserve visible endpoints,
' and list blocker IDs separately from cropped nodes. Use vertical scroll.
' View 3 shows outcomes and in-progress runs. Queued tasks have wait
' reasons and no promised start time. Align timestamps in a fixed
' column across sections. Use muted text for routine timestamps.
' Open on Review queue with task details hidden. Show Changes or Files
' on the left. Press t on a selected task to show its lower-right details.
' Skip the details pane in keyboard navigation while closed or empty.
' Close details if a refresh or view change drops the selected task.
' Show group labels only when they contain tasks. Keep the New instance
' card available in the empty queue. Keep view shortcuts in Help.
' Give the task view and details independent scrolling.
' Key 4 opens Task detail options for the current view. Choose the
' left column, an accordion at the selected task, or a lower-right
' split without opening a closed panel. Show the highlighted t beside
' the task phase with See details or Hide details.
' Press t on a different task to select it and open its details.
' Keep the chosen position across views.
' Anchor the accordion after the selected
' queue row, graph chain, or schedule slot. Use the split for a selection
' without a visible row. Give the split separate scroll regions.
' Keep Enter on a live task bound to attach in each position. Opening a
' file uses the shared preview and returning restores the details position.
'
' ACCEPTANCE FOR A FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION
' Launch two instances from the same pwd and target. Verify disjoint Git
' trees and native history. End them in both orders and resume each by ID
' in a rebuilt VM. Verify failed export, force-kill, retry, stale IDs and
' dropped VM behavior. Check that a stopped or stale instance cannot
' remove another. Check credentials and live process files stay excluded.
' Exercise schedule budget, review feedback, PR revision changes and a
' trip through the native sbx tab while scheduled work keeps running.
' Resize a terminal with a live child. Compare its embedded cursor,
' colors and input handling with stock sbx. Verify switch preserves both
' views and confirming exit restores the host terminal.
' Verify Fresh targets the selected live sandbox when two share a pwd.
' Stop a sandbox and verify its Fresh binding disappears.
' [Unverified] Portable native checkpoint restore across every harness.
' Upstream: https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/#interactive-mode
'           https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/#reconnect-and-name-sandboxes
